{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For the palace.</b> The king abandoned and also forsook the heavy [building], which is not called by a verb's name." "<b>Ophel.</b> A place that was high, from the root of ויעפילו (Numbers 14:44)." "<b>And the bunker.</b> Like 'they stationed it in his bunker' (Isaiah 22:13). They are towers; they were caves."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The text reads הקל ('light') but the corrector's note indicates it should be הכבד ('heavy'); the argument is opaque."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:21.987779444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}